window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b131-45dc08cf67e6663c.json"]={sha256:"45dc08cf67e6663c0b935069a314aa0ecad02819f431befdac00d12de06d85e3",value:{"id":"b131","title":"岩體節理剪力試驗","titleEn":"Rock-joint shear testing","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課聚焦以法向條件、粗糙峰破壞與位移歷程區分節理峰值和殘餘抗剪。沿著調查依據、物理作用、數量估算、現場驗證到工程交接逐項建立可追溯的推論鏈，特別辨別單一數值無法揭露的空間差異及時間效應。以獨立量測檢驗簡化模型，並把觀測結果、教學假設與需要主管工程師審查的決策清楚分列。","summaryEn":"This course focuses on separate peak and residual joint resistance through normal boundaries, asperity damage and displacement history. It develops a traceable reasoning chain from evidence and physical processes through quantitative estimates, field verification and engineering handover. Spatial variation and time effects are separated from a single nominal result. Independent observations test the simplified models, while measured evidence, teaching assumptions and decisions requiring the responsible engineer remain explicitly distinguished.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-investigation","subcategoryTitle":"地質調查與變形監測","subcategoryTitleEn":"Ground investigation and deformation monitoring","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-investigation","learningTags":["underground","ug-investigation","survey"],"architectureFamily":"survey","architectureNodes":[["法向應力與摩擦","Normal stress and friction"],["定力與定剛度邊界","Constant-load and stiffness boundaries"],["峰值與殘餘強度","Peak and residual resistance"],["速率與排水時間","Rate and drainage time"],["剪切功與試後證據","Shear work and post-test evidence"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[3,1]],"diagram":{"type":"survey","labels":["法向應力與摩擦","定力與定剛度邊界","峰值與殘餘強度","速率與排水時間","剪切功與試後證據"],"labelsEn":["Normal stress and friction","Constant-load and stiffness boundaries","Peak and residual resistance","Rate and drainage time","Shear work and post-test evidence"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創教學算例，所有輸入是為比較機制而假設，並非任何地標的實測資料。以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設c=0、σn′=1 MPa、φ=35°，τ=σn′tanφ=0.700 MPa；摩擦角φ降25°時為0.466 MPa。以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設σn=1.2 MPa、u=0.4 MPa，σn′=0.8 MPa；摩擦角φ=30°時抗剪應力τ=0.8tan30°=0.462 MPa。將第一式的一個線性乘數加倍而固定其他邊界，該項貢獻隨之加倍；若為非線性式則必須重新代入，不能等比例外推。把輸入值、單位換算、計算結果及假設列成四欄，再用獨立計算器重算；最後比較量測誤差與模型簡化，判斷改變是否足以支持工程決策。","textEn":"Original teaching example: all inputs are assumptions for comparing mechanisms, not measurements from a landmark project. The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume c=0, σn′=1 MPa and φ=35°; τ=σn′tanφ=0.700 MPa, falling to 0.466 MPa at φ=25°. The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. For assumed σn=1.2 MPa and u=0.4 MPa, σn′=0.8 MPa; at φ=30°, τ=0.8tan30°=0.462 MPa. Doubling one linear multiplicative input in the first relation while holding the remaining boundaries fixed doubles that contribution; a nonlinear relation must instead be evaluated again. Tabulate inputs, unit conversions, results and assumptions in separate columns, and recalculate independently. Finally compare measurement uncertainty with model simplification before deciding whether the difference supports an engineering decision.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b131-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「法向應力與摩擦」與「孔壓與有效法向力」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Normal stress and friction\" and \"Pore pressure and effective normal force\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b131-v14-01","title":"法向應力與摩擦：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Normal stress and friction: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「法向應力與摩擦」如何影響岩體節理剪力試驗的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Normal stress and friction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Rock-joint shear testing”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"節理抗剪力由接觸面法向約束與表面特性共同產生，切向力不應單獨解讀。線性摩擦包絡是指定應力範圍的近似，外推到低應力可能虛構黏聚力，高應力又可能壓碎粗糙峰。 假設c=0、σn′=1 MPa、φ=35°，τ=σn′tanφ=0.700 MPa；摩擦角φ降25°時為0.466 MPa。 不同粗糙度試件混合擬合會產生假的黏聚截距，進而高估低約束節理強度；開挖卸荷後最需要保守判讀的區間反而被外推誤導。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「法向應力與摩擦」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Joint resistance depends on normal confinement and surface condition, not shear force alone. A linear envelope approximates a specified stress range; extrapolation can invent low-stress cohesion or miss asperity crushing under high confinement. Assume c=0, σn′=1 MPa and φ=35°; τ=σn′tanφ=0.700 MPa, falling to 0.466 MPa at φ=25°. Mixing specimens with different roughness can create a false cohesion intercept and overestimate low-confinement resistance, misleading the unloading conditions most relevant beside a newly excavated tunnel. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Normal stress and friction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩點擬合的線性摩擦包絡可以外推到任何法向應力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A linear friction envelope fitted to two points applies at any normal stress.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「法向應力與摩擦」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Normal stress and friction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-01-k1","title":"法向應力與摩擦","titleEn":"Normal stress and friction","text":"節理抗剪力由接觸面法向約束與表面特性共同產生，切向力不應單獨解讀。線性摩擦包絡是指定應力範圍的近似，外推到低應力可能虛構黏聚力，高應力又可能壓碎粗糙峰。","textEn":"Joint resistance depends on normal confinement and surface condition, not shear force alone. A linear envelope approximates a specified stress range; extrapolation can invent low-stress cohesion or miss asperity crushing under high confinement.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩點擬合的線性摩擦包絡可以外推到任何法向應力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A linear friction envelope fitted to two points applies at any normal stress. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「法向應力與摩擦」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Normal stress and friction\" is correct?","options":["兩點擬合的線性摩擦包絡可以外推到任何法向應力。","節理抗剪力由接觸面法向約束與表面特性共同產生，切向力不應單獨解讀。","外加法向荷重除面積就是含水節理的有效法向應力。"],"optionsEn":["A linear friction envelope fitted to two points applies at any normal stress.","Joint resistance depends on normal confinement and surface condition, not shear force alone.","Applied normal load divided by area equals effective stress on a wet joint."],"answer":1,"explanation":"節理抗剪力由接觸面法向約束與表面特性共同產生，切向力不應單獨解讀。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Joint resistance depends on normal confinement and surface condition, not shear force alone. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b131-v14-02","title":"法向應力與摩擦：定量估算","titleEn":"Normal stress and friction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「法向應力與摩擦」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Normal stress and friction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設c=0、σn′=1 MPa、φ=35°，τ=σn′tanφ=0.700 MPa；摩擦角φ降25°時為0.466 MPa。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume c=0, σn′=1 MPa and φ=35°; τ=σn′tanφ=0.700 MPa, falling to 0.466 MPa at φ=25°. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以多個法向應力級試驗並保留完整位移曲線，分別擬合峰值與殘餘值；只有涵蓋設計應力範圍且試件狀態一致的包絡才可交付，不把兩點擬合視為普遍定律。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Test multiple normal stresses and retain complete displacement curves, fitting peak and residual envelopes separately; deliver envelopes only over represented design stresses and consistent specimen conditions rather than treating a two-point fit as universal.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設c=0、σn′=1 MPa、φ=35°，τ=σn′tanφ=0.700 MPa；摩擦角φ降25°時為0.466 MPa。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume c=0, σn′=1 MPa and φ=35°; τ=σn′tanφ=0.700 MPa, falling to 0.466 MPa at φ=25°.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「法向應力與摩擦」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Normal stress and friction\", which statement holds?","options":["只用單側位移計就能完全排除試件轉動造成的假剪脹。","剪切位移增加時，應力仍應永遠除以最初重疊面積。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["One displacement gauge on one side completely excludes rocking-induced false dilation.","Shear stress should always use initial overlap area as displacement increases.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b131-v14-03","title":"法向應力與摩擦：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Normal stress and friction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「法向應力與摩擦」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Normal stress and friction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以多個法向應力級試驗並保留完整位移曲線，分別擬合峰值與殘餘值；只有涵蓋設計應力範圍且試件狀態一致的包絡才可交付，不把兩點擬合視為普遍定律。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：不同粗糙度試件混合擬合會產生假的黏聚截距，進而高估低約束節理強度；開挖卸荷後最需要保守判讀的區間反而被外推誤導。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Test multiple normal stresses and retain complete displacement curves, fitting peak and residual envelopes separately; deliver envelopes only over represented design stresses and consistent specimen conditions rather than treating a two-point fit as universal. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Mixing specimens with different roughness can create a false cohesion intercept and overestimate low-confinement resistance, misleading the unloading conditions most relevant beside a newly excavated tunnel. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄法向應力與摩擦的資料來源與適用條件。以多個法向應力級試驗並保留完整位移曲線，分別擬合峰值與殘餘值；只有涵蓋設計應力範圍且試件狀態一致的包絡才可交付，不把兩點擬合視為普遍定律。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for normal stress and friction. Test multiple normal stresses and retain complete displacement curves, fitting peak and residual envelopes separately; deliver envelopes only over represented design stresses and consistent specimen conditions rather than treating a two-point fit as universal.","failure":"注意干擾：不同粗糙度試件混合擬合會產生假的黏聚截距，進而高估低約束節理強度；開挖卸荷後最需要保守判讀的區間反而被外推誤導。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Mixing specimens with different roughness can create a false cohesion intercept and overestimate low-confinement resistance, misleading the unloading conditions most relevant beside a newly excavated tunnel. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以多個法向應力級試驗並保留完整位移曲線，分別擬合峰值與殘餘值；只有涵蓋設計應力範圍且試件狀態一致的包絡才可交付，不把兩點擬合視為普遍定律。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：不同粗糙度試件混合擬合會產生假的黏聚截距，進而高估低約束節理強度；開挖卸荷後最需要保守判讀的區間反而被外推誤導。","textEn":"Test multiple normal stresses and retain complete displacement curves, fitting peak and residual envelopes separately; deliver envelopes only over represented design stresses and consistent specimen conditions rather than treating a two-point fit as universal. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Mixing specimens with different roughness can create a false cohesion intercept and overestimate low-confinement resistance, misleading the unloading conditions most relevant beside a newly excavated tunnel.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄法向應力與摩擦的資料來源與適用條件。以多個法向應力級試驗並保留完整位移曲線，分別擬合峰值與殘餘值；只有涵蓋設計應力範圍且試件狀態一致的包絡才可交付，不把兩點擬合視為普遍定律。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for normal stress and friction. Test multiple normal stresses and retain complete displacement curves, fitting peak and residual envelopes separately; deliver envelopes only over represented design stresses and consistent specimen conditions rather than treating a two-point fit as universal.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「法向應力與摩擦」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Normal stress and friction\"?","options":["以多個法向應力級試驗並保留完整位移曲線，分別擬合峰值與殘餘值；只有涵蓋設計應力範圍且試件狀態一致的包絡才可交付，不把兩點擬合視為普遍定律。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","一條高解析表面剖面足以代表所有方向和尺度的粗糙度。"],"optionsEn":["Test multiple normal stresses and retain complete displacement curves, fitting peak and residual envelopes separately.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","One high-resolution profile represents roughness in every direction and at every scale."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以多個法向應力級試驗並保留完整位移曲線，分別擬合峰值與殘餘值；只有涵蓋設計應力範圍且試件狀態一致的包絡才可交付，不把兩點擬合視為普遍定律。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Test multiple normal stresses and retain complete displacement curves, fitting peak and residual envelopes separately; deliver envelopes only over represented design stresses and consistent specimen conditions rather than treating a two-point fit as universal. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b131-v14-04","title":"法向應力與摩擦：失效診斷","titleEn":"Normal stress and friction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「法向應力與摩擦」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Normal stress and friction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"不同粗糙度試件混合擬合會產生假的黏聚截距，進而高估低約束節理強度；開挖卸荷後最需要保守判讀的區間反而被外推誤導。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Mixing specimens with different roughness can create a false cohesion intercept and overestimate low-confinement resistance, misleading the unloading conditions most relevant beside a newly excavated tunnel. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：不同粗糙度試件混合擬合會產生假的黏聚截距，進而高估低約束節理強度；開挖卸荷後最需要保守判讀的區間反而被外推誤導。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Mixing specimens with different roughness can create a false cohesion intercept and overestimate low-confinement resistance, misleading the unloading conditions most relevant beside a newly excavated tunnel.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩點擬合的線性摩擦包絡可以外推到任何法向應力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A linear friction envelope fitted to two points applies at any normal stress.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"不同粗糙度試件混合擬合會產生假的黏聚截距，進而高估低約束節理強度；開挖卸荷後最需要保守判讀的區間反而被外推誤導。","textEn":"Mixing specimens with different roughness can create a false cohesion intercept and overestimate low-confinement resistance, misleading the unloading conditions most relevant beside a newly excavated tunnel.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「法向應力與摩擦」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Normal stress and friction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","不同粗糙度試件混合擬合會產生假的黏聚截距，進而高估低約束節理強度；開挖卸荷後最需要保守判讀的區間反而被外推誤導。","外加法向荷重除面積就是含水節理的有效法向應力。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Mixing specimens with different roughness can create a false cohesion intercept and overestimate low-confinement resistance, misleading the unloading conditions most relevant beside a newly excavated tunnel.","Applied normal load divided by area equals effective stress on a wet joint."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同粗糙度試件混合擬合會產生假的黏聚截距，進而高估低約束節理強度；開挖卸荷後最需要保守判讀的區間反而被外推誤導。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Mixing specimens with different roughness can create a false cohesion intercept and overestimate low-confinement resistance, misleading the unloading conditions most relevant beside a newly excavated tunnel. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b131-v14-05","title":"孔壓與有效法向力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Pore pressure and effective normal force: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「孔壓與有效法向力」如何影響岩體節理剪力試驗的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pore pressure and effective normal force” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Rock-joint shear testing”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水壓減少有效接觸約束，但充填物內的孔壓是否均勻取決於排水與載入速率。名義外加法向荷重不等於節理有效法向力，局部未排水反應也不能用遠處水位直接代替。 假設σn=1.2 MPa、u=0.4 MPa，σn′=0.8 MPa；摩擦角φ=30°時抗剪應力τ=0.8tan30°=0.462 MPa。 把總應力代入摩擦式會高估含水弱面強度，孔壓感測器延遲又可能漏掉峰值；試驗看似排水，真正剪切面卻仍可能累積超額孔壓。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「孔壓與有效法向力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Water pressure reduces effective contact confinement, but its distribution through infill depends on drainage and loading rate. Applied normal force is not effective normal force, and a distant water level cannot represent local undrained response. For assumed σn=1.2 MPa and u=0.4 MPa, σn′=0.8 MPa; at φ=30°, τ=0.8tan30°=0.462 MPa. Using total stress overestimates wet-joint strength, and delayed pressure sensing can miss peaks. An apparently drained test may still accumulate excess pressure directly at the shearing surface. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pore pressure and effective normal force” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「外加法向荷重除面積就是含水節理的有效法向應力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Applied normal load divided by area equals effective stress on a wet joint.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「孔壓與有效法向力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pore pressure and effective normal force”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-05-k1","title":"孔壓與有效法向力","titleEn":"Pore pressure and effective normal force","text":"水壓減少有效接觸約束，但充填物內的孔壓是否均勻取決於排水與載入速率。名義外加法向荷重不等於節理有效法向力，局部未排水反應也不能用遠處水位直接代替。","textEn":"Water pressure reduces effective contact confinement, but its distribution through infill depends on drainage and loading rate. Applied normal force is not effective normal force, and a distant water level cannot represent local undrained response.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：外加法向荷重除面積就是含水節理的有效法向應力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Applied normal load divided by area equals effective stress on a wet joint. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「孔壓與有效法向力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pore pressure and effective normal force\" is correct?","options":["外加法向荷重除面積就是含水節理的有效法向應力。","定法向力與定法向剛度試驗必定得到同樣的曲線。","水壓減少有效接觸約束，但充填物內的孔壓是否均勻取決於排水與載入速率。"],"optionsEn":["Applied normal load divided by area equals effective stress on a wet joint.","Constant-normal-load and constant-normal-stiffness tests necessarily produce the same curve.","Water pressure reduces effective contact confinement, but its distribution through infill depends on drainage and loading rate."],"answer":2,"explanation":"水壓減少有效接觸約束，但充填物內的孔壓是否均勻取決於排水與載入速率。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Water pressure reduces effective contact confinement, but its distribution through infill depends on drainage and loading rate. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b131-v14-06","title":"孔壓與有效法向力：定量估算","titleEn":"Pore pressure and effective normal force: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「孔壓與有效法向力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pore pressure and effective normal force” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設σn=1.2 MPa、u=0.4 MPa，σn′=0.8 MPa；摩擦角φ=30°時抗剪應力τ=0.8tan30°=0.462 MPa。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. For assumed σn=1.2 MPa and u=0.4 MPa, σn′=0.8 MPa; at φ=30°, τ=0.8tan30°=0.462 MPa. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將孔壓、法向力及剪力以相同時鐘記錄，檢查排水管線與試體飽和狀態；比較不同速率試驗能否達到同一有效應力路徑，未量到界面孔壓時需明列推估限制。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Synchronize pore pressure, normal force and shear and check drainage and saturation; compare whether different rates achieve the same effective stress path, explicitly limiting results when interface pore pressure is inferred rather than measured.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設σn=1.2 MPa、u=0.4 MPa，σn′=0.8 MPa；摩擦角φ=30°時抗剪應力τ=0.8tan30°=0.462 MPa。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. For assumed σn=1.2 MPa and u=0.4 MPa, σn′=0.8 MPa; at φ=30°, τ=0.8tan30°=0.462 MPa.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「孔壓與有效法向力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pore pressure and effective normal force\", which statement holds?","options":["以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","試驗曲線的最後一點必定已代表真正殘餘強度。","只要試驗速度很慢，就不必再檢查孔壓和排水。"],"optionsEn":["The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","The final point of any test curve necessarily represents true residual strength.","A sufficiently slow test never needs pore-pressure or drainage checks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b131-v14-07","title":"孔壓與有效法向力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pore pressure and effective normal force: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「孔壓與有效法向力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pore pressure and effective normal force” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將孔壓、法向力及剪力以相同時鐘記錄，檢查排水管線與試體飽和狀態；比較不同速率試驗能否達到同一有效應力路徑，未量到界面孔壓時需明列推估限制。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：把總應力代入摩擦式會高估含水弱面強度，孔壓感測器延遲又可能漏掉峰值；試驗看似排水，真正剪切面卻仍可能累積超額孔壓。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Synchronize pore pressure, normal force and shear and check drainage and saturation; compare whether different rates achieve the same effective stress path, explicitly limiting results when interface pore pressure is inferred rather than measured. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Using total stress overestimates wet-joint strength, and delayed pressure sensing can miss peaks. An apparently drained test may still accumulate excess pressure directly at the shearing surface. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄孔壓與有效法向力的資料來源與適用條件。將孔壓、法向力及剪力以相同時鐘記錄，檢查排水管線與試體飽和狀態；比較不同速率試驗能否達到同一有效應力路徑，未量到界面孔壓時需明列推估限制。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for pore pressure and effective normal force. Synchronize pore pressure, normal force and shear and check drainage and saturation; compare whether different rates achieve the same effective stress path, explicitly limiting results when interface pore pressure is inferred rather than measured.","failure":"注意干擾：把總應力代入摩擦式會高估含水弱面強度，孔壓感測器延遲又可能漏掉峰值；試驗看似排水，真正剪切面卻仍可能累積超額孔壓。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using total stress overestimates wet-joint strength, and delayed pressure sensing can miss peaks. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將孔壓、法向力及剪力以相同時鐘記錄，檢查排水管線與試體飽和狀態；比較不同速率試驗能否達到同一有效應力路徑，未量到界面孔壓時需明列推估限制。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：把總應力代入摩擦式會高估含水弱面強度，孔壓感測器延遲又可能漏掉峰值；試驗看似排水，真正剪切面卻仍可能累積超額孔壓。","textEn":"Synchronize pore pressure, normal force and shear and check drainage and saturation; compare whether different rates achieve the same effective stress path, explicitly limiting results when interface pore pressure is inferred rather than measured. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Using total stress overestimates wet-joint strength, and delayed pressure sensing can miss peaks. An apparently drained test may still accumulate excess pressure directly at the shearing surface.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄孔壓與有效法向力的資料來源與適用條件。將孔壓、法向力及剪力以相同時鐘記錄，檢查排水管線與試體飽和狀態；比較不同速率試驗能否達到同一有效應力路徑，未量到界面孔壓時需明列推估限制。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for pore pressure and effective normal force. Synchronize pore pressure, normal force and shear and check drainage and saturation; compare whether different rates achieve the same effective stress path, explicitly limiting results when interface pore pressure is inferred rather than measured.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「孔壓與有效法向力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pore pressure and effective normal force\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","將孔壓、法向力及剪力以相同時鐘記錄，檢查排水管線與試體飽和狀態；比較不同速率試驗能否達到同一有效應力路徑，未量到界面孔壓時需明列推估限制。","力計精度就是整個節理抗剪應力試驗的不確定度。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Synchronize pore pressure, normal force and shear and check drainage and saturation.","Load-cell accuracy equals the complete uncertainty of a joint shear-stress test."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將孔壓、法向力及剪力以相同時鐘記錄，檢查排水管線與試體飽和狀態；比較不同速率試驗能否達到同一有效應力路徑，未量到界面孔壓時需明列推估限制。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Synchronize pore pressure, normal force and shear and check drainage and saturation; compare whether different rates achieve the same effective stress path, explicitly limiting results when interface pore pressure is inferred rather than measured. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b131-v14-08","title":"孔壓與有效法向力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pore pressure and effective normal force: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「孔壓與有效法向力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pore pressure and effective normal force” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把總應力代入摩擦式會高估含水弱面強度，孔壓感測器延遲又可能漏掉峰值；試驗看似排水，真正剪切面卻仍可能累積超額孔壓。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using total stress overestimates wet-joint strength, and delayed pressure sensing can miss peaks. An apparently drained test may still accumulate excess pressure directly at the shearing surface. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把總應力代入摩擦式會高估含水弱面強度，孔壓感測器延遲又可能漏掉峰值；試驗看似排水，真正剪切面卻仍可能累積超額孔壓。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: An apparently drained test may still accumulate excess pressure directly at the shearing surface.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「外加法向荷重除面積就是含水節理的有效法向應力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Applied normal load divided by area equals effective stress on a wet joint.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把總應力代入摩擦式會高估含水弱面強度，孔壓感測器延遲又可能漏掉峰值；試驗看似排水，真正剪切面卻仍可能累積超額孔壓。","textEn":"Using total stress overestimates wet-joint strength, and delayed pressure sensing can miss peaks. An apparently drained test may still accumulate excess pressure directly at the shearing surface.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「孔壓與有效法向力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pore pressure and effective normal force\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","定法向力與定法向剛度試驗必定得到同樣的曲線。","把總應力代入摩擦式會高估含水弱面強度，孔壓感測器延遲又可能漏掉峰值；試驗看似排水，真正剪切面卻仍可能累積超額孔壓。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Constant-normal-load and constant-normal-stiffness tests necessarily produce the same curve.","Using total stress overestimates wet-joint strength, and delayed pressure sensing can miss peaks."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把總應力代入摩擦式會高估含水弱面強度，孔壓感測器延遲又可能漏掉峰值；試驗看似排水，真正剪切面卻仍可能累積超額孔壓。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using total stress overestimates wet-joint strength, and delayed pressure sensing can miss peaks. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b131-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「定力與定剛度邊界」與「剪脹與幾何攀升」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Constant-load and stiffness boundaries\" and \"Dilation and geometric climbing\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b131-v14-09","title":"定力與定剛度邊界：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Constant-load and stiffness boundaries: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「定力與定剛度邊界」如何影響岩體節理剪力試驗的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Constant-load and stiffness boundaries” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Rock-joint shear testing”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"節理剪脹會推動法向邊界，定法向力設備容許位移而保持應力，定剛度邊界則使應力隨剪脹增加。實際圍岩介於不同約束情境，兩種試驗曲線不能直接混成同一材料定律。 假設法向剛度kn=2 MPa/mm、剪脹0.3 mm，Δσn=knΔvn=0.6 MPa；未計設備柔度。 把設備的高剛度效應當成節理本身高強度，會在低約束現地高估承載；控制迴路遲滯則可能製造不實峰值或錯誤剪脹曲線。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「定力與定剛度邊界」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Dilation moves the normal boundary. Constant-normal-load testing permits movement at fixed load, while constant-normal-stiffness testing increases stress as dilation develops. Actual surrounding rock imposes a specific constraint, so the curves are not interchangeable material laws. With assumed normal stiffness kn=2 MPa/mm and dilation 0.3 mm, Δσn=knΔvn=0.6 MPa, excluding machine compliance. Interpreting high machine confinement as intrinsic joint strength overestimates resistance under low field restraint. Controller lag can also create a spurious peak or misleading dilation curve. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Constant-load and stiffness boundaries” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「定法向力與定法向剛度試驗必定得到同樣的曲線。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Constant-normal-load and constant-normal-stiffness tests necessarily produce the same curve.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「定力與定剛度邊界」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Constant-load and stiffness boundaries”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-09-k1","title":"定力與定剛度邊界","titleEn":"Constant-load and stiffness boundaries","text":"節理剪脹會推動法向邊界，定法向力設備容許位移而保持應力，定剛度邊界則使應力隨剪脹增加。實際圍岩介於不同約束情境，兩種試驗曲線不能直接混成同一材料定律。","textEn":"Dilation moves the normal boundary. Constant-normal-load testing permits movement at fixed load, while constant-normal-stiffness testing increases stress as dilation develops.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：定法向力與定法向剛度試驗必定得到同樣的曲線。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Constant-normal-load and constant-normal-stiffness tests necessarily produce the same curve. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「定力與定剛度邊界」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Constant-load and stiffness boundaries\" is correct?","options":["節理剪脹會推動法向邊界，定法向力設備容許位移而保持應力，定剛度邊界則使應力隨剪脹增加。","定法向力與定法向剛度試驗必定得到同樣的曲線。","只用單側位移計就能完全排除試件轉動造成的假剪脹。"],"optionsEn":["Dilation moves the normal boundary.","Constant-normal-load and constant-normal-stiffness tests necessarily produce the same curve.","One displacement gauge on one side completely excludes rocking-induced false dilation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"節理剪脹會推動法向邊界，定法向力設備容許位移而保持應力，定剛度邊界則使應力隨剪脹增加。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Dilation moves the normal boundary. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b131-v14-10","title":"定力與定剛度邊界：定量估算","titleEn":"Constant-load and stiffness boundaries: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「定力與定剛度邊界」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Constant-load and stiffness boundaries” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設法向剛度kn=2 MPa/mm、剪脹0.3 mm，Δσn=knΔvn=0.6 MPa；未計設備柔度。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. With assumed normal stiffness kn=2 MPa/mm and dilation 0.3 mm, Δσn=knΔvn=0.6 MPa, excluding machine compliance. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以標準件校準設備柔度，核對控制器維持的是力、位移還是剛度；將實際法向應力歷程與目標比較，並由設計者說明試驗邊界如何代表隧道周圍岩體。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Calibrate machine compliance with a reference block and verify whether control maintains force, displacement or stiffness; compare actual normal histories with targets and require the designer to justify their representation of surrounding ground.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設法向剛度kn=2 MPa/mm、剪脹0.3 mm，Δσn=knΔvn=0.6 MPa；未計設備柔度。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. With assumed normal stiffness kn=2 MPa/mm and dilation 0.3 mm, Δσn=knΔvn=0.6 MPa, excluding machine compliance.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「定力與定剛度邊界」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Constant-load and stiffness boundaries\", which statement holds?","options":["剪切位移增加時，應力仍應永遠除以最初重疊面積。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","一條高解析表面剖面足以代表所有方向和尺度的粗糙度。"],"optionsEn":["Shear stress should always use initial overlap area as displacement increases.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","One high-resolution profile represents roughness in every direction and at every scale."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b131-v14-11","title":"定力與定剛度邊界：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Constant-load and stiffness boundaries: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「定力與定剛度邊界」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Constant-load and stiffness boundaries” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以標準件校準設備柔度，核對控制器維持的是力、位移還是剛度；將實際法向應力歷程與目標比較，並由設計者說明試驗邊界如何代表隧道周圍岩體。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：把設備的高剛度效應當成節理本身高強度，會在低約束現地高估承載；控制迴路遲滯則可能製造不實峰值或錯誤剪脹曲線。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Calibrate machine compliance with a reference block and verify whether control maintains force, displacement or stiffness; compare actual normal histories with targets and require the designer to justify their representation of surrounding ground. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Interpreting high machine confinement as intrinsic joint strength overestimates resistance under low field restraint. Controller lag can also create a spurious peak or misleading dilation curve. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄定力與定剛度邊界的資料來源與適用條件。以標準件校準設備柔度，核對控制器維持的是力、位移還是剛度；將實際法向應力歷程與目標比較，並由設計者說明試驗邊界如何代表隧道周圍岩體。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for constant-load and stiffness boundaries. Calibrate machine compliance with a reference block and verify whether control maintains force, displacement or stiffness; compare actual normal histories with targets and require the designer to justify their representation of surrounding ground.","failure":"注意干擾：把設備的高剛度效應當成節理本身高強度，會在低約束現地高估承載；控制迴路遲滯則可能製造不實峰值或錯誤剪脹曲線。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Interpreting high machine confinement as intrinsic joint strength overestimates resistance under low field restraint. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以標準件校準設備柔度，核對控制器維持的是力、位移還是剛度；將實際法向應力歷程與目標比較，並由設計者說明試驗邊界如何代表隧道周圍岩體。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：把設備的高剛度效應當成節理本身高強度，會在低約束現地高估承載；控制迴路遲滯則可能製造不實峰值或錯誤剪脹曲線。","textEn":"Calibrate machine compliance with a reference block and verify whether control maintains force, displacement or stiffness; compare actual normal histories with targets and require the designer to justify their representation of surrounding ground. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Interpreting high machine confinement as intrinsic joint strength overestimates resistance under low field restraint. Controller lag can also create a spurious peak or misleading dilation curve.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄定力與定剛度邊界的資料來源與適用條件。以標準件校準設備柔度，核對控制器維持的是力、位移還是剛度；將實際法向應力歷程與目標比較，並由設計者說明試驗邊界如何代表隧道周圍岩體。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for constant-load and stiffness boundaries. Calibrate machine compliance with a reference block and verify whether control maintains force, displacement or stiffness; compare actual normal histories with targets and require the designer to justify their representation of surrounding ground.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「定力與定剛度邊界」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Constant-load and stiffness boundaries\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","剪切曲線下面積全部是目標節理轉成熱的摩擦能。","以標準件校準設備柔度，核對控制器維持的是力、位移還是剛度；將實際法向應力歷程與目標比較，並由設計者說明試驗邊界如何代表隧道周圍岩體。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","All area under the shear curve is frictional heat generated at the intended joint.","Calibrate machine compliance with a reference block and verify whether control maintains force, displacement or stiffness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以標準件校準設備柔度，核對控制器維持的是力、位移還是剛度；將實際法向應力歷程與目標比較，並由設計者說明試驗邊界如何代表隧道周圍岩體。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Calibrate machine compliance with a reference block and verify whether control maintains force, displacement or stiffness; compare actual normal histories with targets and require the designer to justify their representation of surrounding ground. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b131-v14-12","title":"定力與定剛度邊界：失效診斷","titleEn":"Constant-load and stiffness boundaries: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「定力與定剛度邊界」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Constant-load and stiffness boundaries” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把設備的高剛度效應當成節理本身高強度，會在低約束現地高估承載；控制迴路遲滯則可能製造不實峰值或錯誤剪脹曲線。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Interpreting high machine confinement as intrinsic joint strength overestimates resistance under low field restraint. Controller lag can also create a spurious peak or misleading dilation curve. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把設備的高剛度效應當成節理本身高強度，會在低約束現地高估承載；控制迴路遲滯則可能製造不實峰值或錯誤剪脹曲線。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Controller lag can also create a spurious peak or misleading dilation curve.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「定法向力與定法向剛度試驗必定得到同樣的曲線。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Constant-normal-load and constant-normal-stiffness tests necessarily produce the same curve.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把設備的高剛度效應當成節理本身高強度，會在低約束現地高估承載；控制迴路遲滯則可能製造不實峰值或錯誤剪脹曲線。","textEn":"Interpreting high machine confinement as intrinsic joint strength overestimates resistance under low field restraint. Controller lag can also create a spurious peak or misleading dilation curve.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「定力與定剛度邊界」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Constant-load and stiffness boundaries\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把設備的高剛度效應當成節理本身高強度，會在低約束現地高估承載；控制迴路遲滯則可能製造不實峰值或錯誤剪脹曲線。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","只用單側位移計就能完全排除試件轉動造成的假剪脹。"],"optionsEn":["Interpreting high machine confinement as intrinsic joint strength overestimates resistance under low field restraint.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","One displacement gauge on one side completely excludes rocking-induced false dilation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把設備的高剛度效應當成節理本身高強度，會在低約束現地高估承載；控制迴路遲滯則可能製造不實峰值或錯誤剪脹曲線。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Interpreting high machine confinement as intrinsic joint strength overestimates resistance under low field restraint. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b131-v14-13","title":"剪脹與幾何攀升：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Dilation and geometric climbing: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「剪脹與幾何攀升」如何影響岩體節理剪力試驗的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Dilation and geometric climbing” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Rock-joint shear testing”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"粗糙峰互相攀升造成剪脹，同時提高切向阻力；隨法向應力增加，峰體可能剪斷而減少幾何攀升。剪脹角是位移路徑斜率，不能當成所有位移階段固定的摩擦增量。 假設剪移2 mm產生法向增量0.2 mm，ψ=atan(0.2/2)=5.71°；此為該段平均角。 試件轉動可假裝成剪脹，若用此角度提高強度會造成雙重高估；剪後磨平卻仍沿用初始剪脹角，也會錯估大位移殘餘行為。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「剪脹與幾何攀升」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Asperities climb over one another, generating dilation and additional resistance. Greater confinement may shear them off and reduce climbing. Dilation angle is a displacement-path slope, not a constant friction increment throughout the test. Assume 2 mm shear displacement produces 0.2 mm normal movement; ψ=atan(0.2/2)=5.71°, averaged only over that interval. Specimen rotation can masquerade as dilation and falsely increase inferred resistance. Retaining initial dilation after the surface has polished also misrepresents large-displacement residual behavior. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Dilation and geometric climbing” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「只用單側位移計就能完全排除試件轉動造成的假剪脹。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"One displacement gauge on one side completely excludes rocking-induced false dilation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「剪脹與幾何攀升」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Dilation and geometric climbing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-13-k1","title":"剪脹與幾何攀升","titleEn":"Dilation and geometric climbing","text":"粗糙峰互相攀升造成剪脹，同時提高切向阻力；隨法向應力增加，峰體可能剪斷而減少幾何攀升。剪脹角是位移路徑斜率，不能當成所有位移階段固定的摩擦增量。","textEn":"Asperities climb over one another, generating dilation and additional resistance. Greater confinement may shear them off and reduce climbing.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只用單側位移計就能完全排除試件轉動造成的假剪脹。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: One displacement gauge on one side completely excludes rocking-induced false dilation. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「剪脹與幾何攀升」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Dilation and geometric climbing\" is correct?","options":["只用單側位移計就能完全排除試件轉動造成的假剪脹。","粗糙峰互相攀升造成剪脹，同時提高切向阻力；隨法向應力增加，峰體可能剪斷而減少幾何攀升。","試驗曲線的最後一點必定已代表真正殘餘強度。"],"optionsEn":["One displacement gauge on one side completely excludes rocking-induced false dilation.","Asperities climb over one another, generating dilation and additional resistance.","The final point of any test curve necessarily represents true residual strength."],"answer":1,"explanation":"粗糙峰互相攀升造成剪脹，同時提高切向阻力；隨法向應力增加，峰體可能剪斷而減少幾何攀升。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Asperities climb over one another, generating dilation and additional resistance. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b131-v14-14","title":"剪脹與幾何攀升：定量估算","titleEn":"Dilation and geometric climbing: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「剪脹與幾何攀升」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Dilation and geometric climbing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設剪移2 mm產生法向增量0.2 mm，ψ=atan(0.2/2)=5.71°；此為該段平均角。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume 2 mm shear displacement produces 0.2 mm normal movement; ψ=atan(0.2/2)=5.71°, averaged only over that interval. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用雙側位移計檢查試件傾斜，逐段求法向對剪向位移斜率；比較剪後表面與碎屑，判定剪脹降低是粗糙峰破壞或儀器轉動，不能只看一支量規。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use displacement gauges on both sides to detect rocking and evaluate incremental slopes; compare post-test surfaces and debris to distinguish asperity damage from instrument rotation rather than relying on one gauge.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設剪移2 mm產生法向增量0.2 mm，ψ=atan(0.2/2)=5.71°；此為該段平均角。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume 2 mm shear displacement produces 0.2 mm normal movement; ψ=atan(0.2/2)=5.71°, averaged only over that interval.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「剪脹與幾何攀升」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Dilation and geometric climbing\", which statement holds?","options":["只要試驗速度很慢，就不必再檢查孔壓和排水。","力計精度就是整個節理抗剪應力試驗的不確定度。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["A sufficiently slow test never needs pore-pressure or drainage checks.","Load-cell accuracy equals the complete uncertainty of a joint shear-stress test.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b131-v14-15","title":"剪脹與幾何攀升：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Dilation and geometric climbing: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「剪脹與幾何攀升」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Dilation and geometric climbing” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用雙側位移計檢查試件傾斜，逐段求法向對剪向位移斜率；比較剪後表面與碎屑，判定剪脹降低是粗糙峰破壞或儀器轉動，不能只看一支量規。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：試件轉動可假裝成剪脹，若用此角度提高強度會造成雙重高估；剪後磨平卻仍沿用初始剪脹角，也會錯估大位移殘餘行為。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use displacement gauges on both sides to detect rocking and evaluate incremental slopes; compare post-test surfaces and debris to distinguish asperity damage from instrument rotation rather than relying on one gauge. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Specimen rotation can masquerade as dilation and falsely increase inferred resistance. Retaining initial dilation after the surface has polished also misrepresents large-displacement residual behavior. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄剪脹與幾何攀升的資料來源與適用條件。用雙側位移計檢查試件傾斜，逐段求法向對剪向位移斜率；比較剪後表面與碎屑，判定剪脹降低是粗糙峰破壞或儀器轉動，不能只看一支量規。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for dilation and geometric climbing. Use displacement gauges on both sides to detect rocking and evaluate incremental slopes; compare post-test surfaces and debris to distinguish asperity damage from instrument rotation rather than relying on one gauge.","failure":"注意干擾：試件轉動可假裝成剪脹，若用此角度提高強度會造成雙重高估；剪後磨平卻仍沿用初始剪脹角，也會錯估大位移殘餘行為。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Specimen rotation can masquerade as dilation and falsely increase inferred resistance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用雙側位移計檢查試件傾斜，逐段求法向對剪向位移斜率；比較剪後表面與碎屑，判定剪脹降低是粗糙峰破壞或儀器轉動，不能只看一支量規。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：試件轉動可假裝成剪脹，若用此角度提高強度會造成雙重高估；剪後磨平卻仍沿用初始剪脹角，也會錯估大位移殘餘行為。","textEn":"Use displacement gauges on both sides to detect rocking and evaluate incremental slopes; compare post-test surfaces and debris to distinguish asperity damage from instrument rotation rather than relying on one gauge. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Specimen rotation can masquerade as dilation and falsely increase inferred resistance. Retaining initial dilation after the surface has polished also misrepresents large-displacement residual behavior.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄剪脹與幾何攀升的資料來源與適用條件。用雙側位移計檢查試件傾斜，逐段求法向對剪向位移斜率；比較剪後表面與碎屑，判定剪脹降低是粗糙峰破壞或儀器轉動，不能只看一支量規。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for dilation and geometric climbing. Use displacement gauges on both sides to detect rocking and evaluate incremental slopes; compare post-test surfaces and debris to distinguish asperity damage from instrument rotation rather than relying on one gauge.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「剪脹與幾何攀升」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Dilation and geometric climbing\"?","options":["用雙側位移計檢查試件傾斜，逐段求法向對剪向位移斜率；比較剪後表面與碎屑，判定剪脹降低是粗糙峰破壞或儀器轉動，不能只看一支量規。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","兩點擬合的線性摩擦包絡可以外推到任何法向應力。"],"optionsEn":["Use displacement gauges on both sides to detect rocking and evaluate incremental slopes.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A linear friction envelope fitted to two points applies at any normal stress."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用雙側位移計檢查試件傾斜，逐段求法向對剪向位移斜率；比較剪後表面與碎屑，判定剪脹降低是粗糙峰破壞或儀器轉動，不能只看一支量規。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use displacement gauges on both sides to detect rocking and evaluate incremental slopes; compare post-test surfaces and debris to distinguish asperity damage from instrument rotation rather than relying on one gauge. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b131-v14-16","title":"剪脹與幾何攀升：失效診斷","titleEn":"Dilation and geometric climbing: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「剪脹與幾何攀升」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Dilation and geometric climbing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"試件轉動可假裝成剪脹，若用此角度提高強度會造成雙重高估；剪後磨平卻仍沿用初始剪脹角，也會錯估大位移殘餘行為。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Specimen rotation can masquerade as dilation and falsely increase inferred resistance. Retaining initial dilation after the surface has polished also misrepresents large-displacement residual behavior. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：試件轉動可假裝成剪脹，若用此角度提高強度會造成雙重高估；剪後磨平卻仍沿用初始剪脹角，也會錯估大位移殘餘行為。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Retaining initial dilation after the surface has polished also misrepresents large-displacement residual behavior.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只用單側位移計就能完全排除試件轉動造成的假剪脹。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"One displacement gauge on one side completely excludes rocking-induced false dilation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"試件轉動可假裝成剪脹，若用此角度提高強度會造成雙重高估；剪後磨平卻仍沿用初始剪脹角，也會錯估大位移殘餘行為。","textEn":"Specimen rotation can masquerade as dilation and falsely increase inferred resistance. Retaining initial dilation after the surface has polished also misrepresents large-displacement residual behavior.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「剪脹與幾何攀升」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Dilation and geometric climbing\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","試件轉動可假裝成剪脹，若用此角度提高強度會造成雙重高估；剪後磨平卻仍沿用初始剪脹角，也會錯估大位移殘餘行為。","試驗曲線的最後一點必定已代表真正殘餘強度。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Specimen rotation can masquerade as dilation and falsely increase inferred resistance.","The final point of any test curve necessarily represents true residual strength."],"answer":1,"explanation":"試件轉動可假裝成剪脹，若用此角度提高強度會造成雙重高估；剪後磨平卻仍沿用初始剪脹角，也會錯估大位移殘餘行為。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Specimen rotation can masquerade as dilation and falsely increase inferred resistance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b131-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「峰值與殘餘強度」與「剪切面積修正」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Peak and residual resistance\" and \"Shearing-area correction\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b131-v14-17","title":"峰值與殘餘強度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Peak and residual resistance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「峰值與殘餘強度」如何影響岩體節理剪力試驗的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Peak and residual resistance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Rock-joint shear testing”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"峰值需要原有咬合或膠結尚未破壞，殘餘強度則對應較大位移後形成的滑動面。隧道附近若已有位移歷史，直接採首次峰值可能不適當，應先辨識設計機制需要哪一段。 假設峰值0.9 MPa、殘餘0.5 MPa，峰後降幅(0.9−0.5)/0.9=44.4%；不是安全係數。 試驗行程不足時末端值不一定是殘餘值，重複使用磨損面又會低估首次峰值；若未記錄試件歷史，兩種錯誤都可能混入同一資料庫。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「峰值與殘餘強度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Peak resistance depends on surviving interlock or bonding, while residual resistance follows development of a sliding surface. Previously displaced ground may not mobilize a first-cycle peak, so the required part of the curve depends on the design mechanism. Assumed peak and residual stresses of 0.9 and 0.5 MPa give a post-peak drop of 44.4%; this is not a factor of safety. Insufficient travel means the final reading may not be residual, while reusing a worn surface understates the first peak. Without specimen history both errors can enter one apparently consistent database. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Peak and residual resistance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「試驗曲線的最後一點必定已代表真正殘餘強度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The final point of any test curve necessarily represents true residual strength.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「峰值與殘餘強度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Peak and residual resistance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-17-k1","title":"峰值與殘餘強度","titleEn":"Peak and residual resistance","text":"峰值需要原有咬合或膠結尚未破壞，殘餘強度則對應較大位移後形成的滑動面。隧道附近若已有位移歷史，直接採首次峰值可能不適當，應先辨識設計機制需要哪一段。","textEn":"Peak resistance depends on surviving interlock or bonding, while residual resistance follows development of a sliding surface. Previously displaced ground may not mobilize a first-cycle peak, so the required part of the curve depends on the design mechanism.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：試驗曲線的最後一點必定已代表真正殘餘強度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The final point of any test curve necessarily represents true residual strength. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「峰值與殘餘強度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Peak and residual resistance\" is correct?","options":["試驗曲線的最後一點必定已代表真正殘餘強度。","剪切位移增加時，應力仍應永遠除以最初重疊面積。","峰值需要原有咬合或膠結尚未破壞，殘餘強度則對應較大位移後形成的滑動面。"],"optionsEn":["The final point of any test curve necessarily represents true residual strength.","Shear stress should always use initial overlap area as displacement increases.","Peak resistance depends on surviving interlock or bonding, while residual resistance follows development of a sliding surface."],"answer":2,"explanation":"峰值需要原有咬合或膠結尚未破壞，殘餘強度則對應較大位移後形成的滑動面。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Peak resistance depends on surviving interlock or bonding, while residual resistance follows development of a sliding surface. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b131-v14-18","title":"峰值與殘餘強度：定量估算","titleEn":"Peak and residual resistance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「峰值與殘餘強度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Peak and residual resistance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設峰值0.9 MPa、殘餘0.5 MPa，峰後降幅(0.9−0.5)/0.9=44.4%；不是安全係數。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assumed peak and residual stresses of 0.9 and 0.5 MPa give a post-peak drop of 44.4%; this is not a factor of safety. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：保留足夠位移範圍的曲線並檢查是否真正進入穩定滑動，註記試件先前剪切與方向；設計參數表應分列峰值、軟化過程和殘餘，不以一個平均值替代。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Retain curves over enough displacement to assess stable sliding and document prior shearing and direction; parameter tables distinguish peak, softening and residual behavior rather than replacing all three with one average.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設峰值0.9 MPa、殘餘0.5 MPa，峰後降幅(0.9−0.5)/0.9=44.4%；不是安全係數。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assumed peak and residual stresses of 0.9 and 0.5 MPa give a post-peak drop of 44.4%; this is not a factor of safety.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「峰值與殘餘強度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Peak and residual resistance\", which statement holds?","options":["以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","一條高解析表面剖面足以代表所有方向和尺度的粗糙度。","剪切曲線下面積全部是目標節理轉成熱的摩擦能。"],"optionsEn":["The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","One high-resolution profile represents roughness in every direction and at every scale.","All area under the shear curve is frictional heat generated at the intended joint."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b131-v14-19","title":"峰值與殘餘強度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Peak and residual resistance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「峰值與殘餘強度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Peak and residual resistance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"保留足夠位移範圍的曲線並檢查是否真正進入穩定滑動，註記試件先前剪切與方向；設計參數表應分列峰值、軟化過程和殘餘，不以一個平均值替代。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：試驗行程不足時末端值不一定是殘餘值，重複使用磨損面又會低估首次峰值；若未記錄試件歷史，兩種錯誤都可能混入同一資料庫。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Retain curves over enough displacement to assess stable sliding and document prior shearing and direction; parameter tables distinguish peak, softening and residual behavior rather than replacing all three with one average. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Insufficient travel means the final reading may not be residual, while reusing a worn surface understates the first peak. Without specimen history both errors can enter one apparently consistent database. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄峰值與殘餘強度的資料來源與適用條件。保留足夠位移範圍的曲線並檢查是否真正進入穩定滑動，註記試件先前剪切與方向；設計參數表應分列峰值、軟化過程和殘餘，不以一個平均值替代。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for peak and residual resistance. Retain curves over enough displacement to assess stable sliding and document prior shearing and direction; parameter tables distinguish peak, softening and residual behavior rather than replacing all three with one average.","failure":"注意干擾：試驗行程不足時末端值不一定是殘餘值，重複使用磨損面又會低估首次峰值；若未記錄試件歷史，兩種錯誤都可能混入同一資料庫。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Insufficient travel means the final reading may not be residual, while reusing a worn surface understates the first peak. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"保留足夠位移範圍的曲線並檢查是否真正進入穩定滑動，註記試件先前剪切與方向；設計參數表應分列峰值、軟化過程和殘餘，不以一個平均值替代。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：試驗行程不足時末端值不一定是殘餘值，重複使用磨損面又會低估首次峰值；若未記錄試件歷史，兩種錯誤都可能混入同一資料庫。","textEn":"Retain curves over enough displacement to assess stable sliding and document prior shearing and direction; parameter tables distinguish peak, softening and residual behavior rather than replacing all three with one average. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Insufficient travel means the final reading may not be residual, while reusing a worn surface understates the first peak. Without specimen history both errors can enter one apparently consistent database.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄峰值與殘餘強度的資料來源與適用條件。保留足夠位移範圍的曲線並檢查是否真正進入穩定滑動，註記試件先前剪切與方向；設計參數表應分列峰值、軟化過程和殘餘，不以一個平均值替代。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for peak and residual resistance. Retain curves over enough displacement to assess stable sliding and document prior shearing and direction; parameter tables distinguish peak, softening and residual behavior rather than replacing all three with one average.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「峰值與殘餘強度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Peak and residual resistance\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","保留足夠位移範圍的曲線並檢查是否真正進入穩定滑動，註記試件先前剪切與方向；設計參數表應分列峰值、軟化過程和殘餘，不以一個平均值替代。","外加法向荷重除面積就是含水節理的有效法向應力。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Retain curves over enough displacement to assess stable sliding and document prior shearing and direction.","Applied normal load divided by area equals effective stress on a wet joint."],"answer":1,"explanation":"保留足夠位移範圍的曲線並檢查是否真正進入穩定滑動，註記試件先前剪切與方向；設計參數表應分列峰值、軟化過程和殘餘，不以一個平均值替代。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Retain curves over enough displacement to assess stable sliding and document prior shearing and direction; parameter tables distinguish peak, softening and residual behavior rather than replacing all three with one average. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b131-v14-20","title":"峰值與殘餘強度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Peak and residual resistance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「峰值與殘餘強度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Peak and residual resistance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"試驗行程不足時末端值不一定是殘餘值，重複使用磨損面又會低估首次峰值；若未記錄試件歷史，兩種錯誤都可能混入同一資料庫。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Insufficient travel means the final reading may not be residual, while reusing a worn surface understates the first peak. Without specimen history both errors can enter one apparently consistent database. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：試驗行程不足時末端值不一定是殘餘值，重複使用磨損面又會低估首次峰值；若未記錄試件歷史，兩種錯誤都可能混入同一資料庫。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Without specimen history both errors can enter one apparently consistent database.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「試驗曲線的最後一點必定已代表真正殘餘強度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The final point of any test curve necessarily represents true residual strength.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"試驗行程不足時末端值不一定是殘餘值，重複使用磨損面又會低估首次峰值；若未記錄試件歷史，兩種錯誤都可能混入同一資料庫。","textEn":"Insufficient travel means the final reading may not be residual, while reusing a worn surface understates the first peak. Without specimen history both errors can enter one apparently consistent database.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「峰值與殘餘強度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Peak and residual resistance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","剪切位移增加時，應力仍應永遠除以最初重疊面積。","試驗行程不足時末端值不一定是殘餘值，重複使用磨損面又會低估首次峰值；若未記錄試件歷史，兩種錯誤都可能混入同一資料庫。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Shear stress should always use initial overlap area as displacement increases.","Insufficient travel means the final reading may not be residual, while reusing a worn surface understates the first peak."],"answer":2,"explanation":"試驗行程不足時末端值不一定是殘餘值，重複使用磨損面又會低估首次峰值；若未記錄試件歷史，兩種錯誤都可能混入同一資料庫。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Insufficient travel means the final reading may not be residual, while reusing a worn surface understates the first peak. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b131-v14-21","title":"剪切面積修正：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Shearing-area correction: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「剪切面積修正」如何影響岩體節理剪力試驗的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Shearing-area correction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Rock-joint shear testing”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"剪切位移增加會減少上下試件的重疊面積，若仍以初始面積換算應力，就把幾何變化混入材料軟化。對不規則天然節理還需考慮實際接觸區，名義重疊不等於真實接觸。 假設矩形100×100 mm試件剪移10 mm，重疊9000 mm²；剪力9 kN對應1.0 MPa，初始面積算法為0.9 MPa。 忽略面積縮小會把實際穩定阻力誤判為軟化，重複做面積修正又會高估強度；兩者在大位移段尤為嚴重並影響殘餘值。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「剪切面積修正」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Shear movement reduces specimen overlap, so initial-area stress mixes geometry with material softening. Irregular natural joints also have evolving contact patches; nominal overlap is not the true contact area resisting shear. An assumed 100×100 mm specimen displaced 10 mm has 9000 mm² overlap; 9 kN gives 1.0 MPa instead of 0.9 MPa using initial area. Ignoring reduced area can make stable resistance appear to soften, while applying correction twice overestimates strength. Both errors become pronounced at large displacement and bias residual values. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Shearing-area correction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「剪切位移增加時，應力仍應永遠除以最初重疊面積。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Shear stress should always use initial overlap area as displacement increases.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「剪切面積修正」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Shearing-area correction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-21-k1","title":"剪切面積修正","titleEn":"Shearing-area correction","text":"剪切位移增加會減少上下試件的重疊面積，若仍以初始面積換算應力，就把幾何變化混入材料軟化。對不規則天然節理還需考慮實際接觸區，名義重疊不等於真實接觸。","textEn":"Shear movement reduces specimen overlap, so initial-area stress mixes geometry with material softening. Irregular natural joints also have evolving contact patches; nominal overlap is not the true contact area resisting shear.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：剪切位移增加時，應力仍應永遠除以最初重疊面積。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Shear stress should always use initial overlap area as displacement increases. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「剪切面積修正」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Shearing-area correction\" is correct?","options":["剪切位移增加會減少上下試件的重疊面積，若仍以初始面積換算應力，就把幾何變化混入材料軟化。","剪切位移增加時，應力仍應永遠除以最初重疊面積。","只要試驗速度很慢，就不必再檢查孔壓和排水。"],"optionsEn":["Shear movement reduces specimen overlap, so initial-area stress mixes geometry with material softening.","Shear stress should always use initial overlap area as displacement increases.","A sufficiently slow test never needs pore-pressure or drainage checks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"剪切位移增加會減少上下試件的重疊面積，若仍以初始面積換算應力，就把幾何變化混入材料軟化。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Shear movement reduces specimen overlap, so initial-area stress mixes geometry with material softening. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b131-v14-22","title":"剪切面積修正：定量估算","titleEn":"Shearing-area correction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「剪切面積修正」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Shearing-area correction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設矩形100×100 mm試件剪移10 mm，重疊9000 mm²；剪力9 kN對應1.0 MPa，初始面積算法為0.9 MPa。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. An assumed 100×100 mm specimen displaced 10 mm has 9000 mm² overlap; 9 kN gives 1.0 MPa instead of 0.9 MPa using initial area. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：從試件幾何與實測位移逐點重算名義面積，並保存未修正與修正應力曲線；若天然表面接觸範圍未知，說明名義面積定義，不用影像猜出的接觸率任意再放大應力。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Recalculate nominal area at each measured displacement and retain corrected and uncorrected curves; if natural contact area is unknown, state the nominal definition rather than arbitrarily amplifying stress through a guessed contact fraction.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設矩形100×100 mm試件剪移10 mm，重疊9000 mm²；剪力9 kN對應1.0 MPa，初始面積算法為0.9 MPa。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. An assumed 100×100 mm specimen displaced 10 mm has 9000 mm² overlap; 9 kN gives 1.0 MPa instead of 0.9 MPa using initial area.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「剪切面積修正」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Shearing-area correction\", which statement holds?","options":["力計精度就是整個節理抗剪應力試驗的不確定度。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","兩點擬合的線性摩擦包絡可以外推到任何法向應力。"],"optionsEn":["Load-cell accuracy equals the complete uncertainty of a joint shear-stress test.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","A linear friction envelope fitted to two points applies at any normal stress."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b131-v14-23","title":"剪切面積修正：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Shearing-area correction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「剪切面積修正」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Shearing-area correction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"從試件幾何與實測位移逐點重算名義面積，並保存未修正與修正應力曲線；若天然表面接觸範圍未知，說明名義面積定義，不用影像猜出的接觸率任意再放大應力。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：忽略面積縮小會把實際穩定阻力誤判為軟化，重複做面積修正又會高估強度；兩者在大位移段尤為嚴重並影響殘餘值。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Recalculate nominal area at each measured displacement and retain corrected and uncorrected curves; if natural contact area is unknown, state the nominal definition rather than arbitrarily amplifying stress through a guessed contact fraction. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Ignoring reduced area can make stable resistance appear to soften, while applying correction twice overestimates strength. Both errors become pronounced at large displacement and bias residual values. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄剪切面積修正的資料來源與適用條件。從試件幾何與實測位移逐點重算名義面積，並保存未修正與修正應力曲線；若天然表面接觸範圍未知，說明名義面積定義，不用影像猜出的接觸率任意再放大應力。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for shearing-area correction. Recalculate nominal area at each measured displacement and retain corrected and uncorrected curves; if natural contact area is unknown, state the nominal definition rather than arbitrarily amplifying stress through a guessed contact fraction.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略面積縮小會把實際穩定阻力誤判為軟化，重複做面積修正又會高估強度；兩者在大位移段尤為嚴重並影響殘餘值。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring reduced area can make stable resistance appear to soften, while applying correction twice overestimates strength. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"從試件幾何與實測位移逐點重算名義面積，並保存未修正與修正應力曲線；若天然表面接觸範圍未知，說明名義面積定義，不用影像猜出的接觸率任意再放大應力。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：忽略面積縮小會把實際穩定阻力誤判為軟化，重複做面積修正又會高估強度；兩者在大位移段尤為嚴重並影響殘餘值。","textEn":"Recalculate nominal area at each measured displacement and retain corrected and uncorrected curves; if natural contact area is unknown, state the nominal definition rather than arbitrarily amplifying stress through a guessed contact fraction. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Ignoring reduced area can make stable resistance appear to soften, while applying correction twice overestimates strength. Both errors become pronounced at large displacement and bias residual values.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄剪切面積修正的資料來源與適用條件。從試件幾何與實測位移逐點重算名義面積，並保存未修正與修正應力曲線；若天然表面接觸範圍未知，說明名義面積定義，不用影像猜出的接觸率任意再放大應力。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for shearing-area correction. Recalculate nominal area at each measured displacement and retain corrected and uncorrected curves; if natural contact area is unknown, state the nominal definition rather than arbitrarily amplifying stress through a guessed contact fraction.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「剪切面積修正」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Shearing-area correction\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","定法向力與定法向剛度試驗必定得到同樣的曲線。","從試件幾何與實測位移逐點重算名義面積，並保存未修正與修正應力曲線；若天然表面接觸範圍未知，說明名義面積定義，不用影像猜出的接觸率任意再放大應力。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Constant-normal-load and constant-normal-stiffness tests necessarily produce the same curve.","Recalculate nominal area at each measured displacement and retain corrected and uncorrected curves."],"answer":2,"explanation":"從試件幾何與實測位移逐點重算名義面積，並保存未修正與修正應力曲線；若天然表面接觸範圍未知，說明名義面積定義，不用影像猜出的接觸率任意再放大應力。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Recalculate nominal area at each measured displacement and retain corrected and uncorrected curves; if natural contact area is unknown, state the nominal definition rather than arbitrarily amplifying stress through a guessed contact fraction. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b131-v14-24","title":"剪切面積修正：失效診斷","titleEn":"Shearing-area correction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「剪切面積修正」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Shearing-area correction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略面積縮小會把實際穩定阻力誤判為軟化，重複做面積修正又會高估強度；兩者在大位移段尤為嚴重並影響殘餘值。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring reduced area can make stable resistance appear to soften, while applying correction twice overestimates strength. Both errors become pronounced at large displacement and bias residual values. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：忽略面積縮小會把實際穩定阻力誤判為軟化，重複做面積修正又會高估強度；兩者在大位移段尤為嚴重並影響殘餘值。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Both errors become pronounced at large displacement and bias residual values.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「剪切位移增加時，應力仍應永遠除以最初重疊面積。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Shear stress should always use initial overlap area as displacement increases.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略面積縮小會把實際穩定阻力誤判為軟化，重複做面積修正又會高估強度；兩者在大位移段尤為嚴重並影響殘餘值。","textEn":"Ignoring reduced area can make stable resistance appear to soften, while applying correction twice overestimates strength. Both errors become pronounced at large displacement and bias residual values.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「剪切面積修正」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Shearing-area correction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["忽略面積縮小會把實際穩定阻力誤判為軟化，重複做面積修正又會高估強度；兩者在大位移段尤為嚴重並影響殘餘值。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","只要試驗速度很慢，就不必再檢查孔壓和排水。"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring reduced area can make stable resistance appear to soften, while applying correction twice overestimates strength.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","A sufficiently slow test never needs pore-pressure or drainage checks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"忽略面積縮小會把實際穩定阻力誤判為軟化，重複做面積修正又會高估強度；兩者在大位移段尤為嚴重並影響殘餘值。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring reduced area can make stable resistance appear to soften, while applying correction twice overestimates strength. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b131-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「速率與排水時間」與「粗糙度與尺度差」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Rate and drainage time\" and \"Roughness and scale dependence\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b131-v14-25","title":"速率與排水時間：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Rate and drainage time: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「速率與排水時間」如何影響岩體節理剪力試驗的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Rate and drainage time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Rock-joint shear testing”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"細粒充填的排水時間取決於排水距離和固結係數，剪切太快會改變孔壓而非只改變摩擦。岩石接觸面也可能有速率效應，所以速度比較必須維持相同水文與正向約束。 假設特徵排水距離5 mm、cv=10⁻⁸ m²/s，t=L²/cv=2500 s約41.7 min；此為尺度估算。 將未排水弱化歸因於表面磨耗會選錯殘餘參數，反之緩慢試驗的高阻力也不能代表快速卸荷；缺少孔壓資料時兩種機制很難分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「速率與排水時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Fine infill drainage depends on path length and consolidation coefficient; rapid shearing changes pore pressure as well as friction. Rock contacts may themselves be rate sensitive, so rate comparisons need matched hydraulic and normal boundaries. For assumed drainage length 5 mm and cv=10⁻⁸ m²/s, t=L²/cv=2500 s, about 41.7 min; this is a scaling estimate. Attributing undrained weakening to surface wear selects the wrong residual parameter, while slow-test resistance does not represent rapid unloading. Without pore-pressure records the mechanisms are difficult to distinguish. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rate and drainage time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要試驗速度很慢，就不必再檢查孔壓和排水。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A sufficiently slow test never needs pore-pressure or drainage checks.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「速率與排水時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Rate and drainage time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-25-k1","title":"速率與排水時間","titleEn":"Rate and drainage time","text":"細粒充填的排水時間取決於排水距離和固結係數，剪切太快會改變孔壓而非只改變摩擦。岩石接觸面也可能有速率效應，所以速度比較必須維持相同水文與正向約束。","textEn":"Fine infill drainage depends on path length and consolidation coefficient; rapid shearing changes pore pressure as well as friction. Rock contacts may themselves be rate sensitive, so rate comparisons need matched hydraulic and normal boundaries.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要試驗速度很慢，就不必再檢查孔壓和排水。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A sufficiently slow test never needs pore-pressure or drainage checks. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「速率與排水時間」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Rate and drainage time\" is correct?","options":["只要試驗速度很慢，就不必再檢查孔壓和排水。","細粒充填的排水時間取決於排水距離和固結係數，剪切太快會改變孔壓而非只改變摩擦。","一條高解析表面剖面足以代表所有方向和尺度的粗糙度。"],"optionsEn":["A sufficiently slow test never needs pore-pressure or drainage checks.","Fine infill drainage depends on path length and consolidation coefficient; rapid shearing changes pore pressure as well as friction.","One high-resolution profile represents roughness in every direction and at every scale."],"answer":1,"explanation":"細粒充填的排水時間取決於排水距離和固結係數，剪切太快會改變孔壓而非只改變摩擦。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Fine infill drainage depends on path length and consolidation coefficient; rapid shearing changes pore pressure as well as friction. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b131-v14-26","title":"速率與排水時間：定量估算","titleEn":"Rate and drainage time: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「速率與排水時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Rate and drainage time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設特徵排水距離5 mm、cv=10⁻⁸ m²/s，t=L²/cv=2500 s約41.7 min；此為尺度估算。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. For assumed drainage length 5 mm and cv=10⁻⁸ m²/s, t=L²/cv=2500 s, about 41.7 min; this is a scaling estimate. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較剪切時間與排水尺度並監測孔壓，使用不同速度時保持相同飽和與邊界；試驗方案由專業人員選定，課程時間估算不能替代規範要求或直接成為設備速率設定。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare shearing duration with drainage scale while monitoring pressure, holding saturation and boundaries constant across rates; specialists select the test program, and this time estimate does not prescribe a machine rate or replace a standard.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設特徵排水距離5 mm、cv=10⁻⁸ m²/s，t=L²/cv=2500 s約41.7 min；此為尺度估算。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. For assumed drainage length 5 mm and cv=10⁻⁸ m²/s, t=L²/cv=2500 s, about 41.7 min; this is a scaling estimate.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「速率與排水時間」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Rate and drainage time\", which statement holds?","options":["剪切曲線下面積全部是目標節理轉成熱的摩擦能。","外加法向荷重除面積就是含水節理的有效法向應力。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["All area under the shear curve is frictional heat generated at the intended joint.","Applied normal load divided by area equals effective stress on a wet joint.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b131-v14-27","title":"速率與排水時間：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Rate and drainage time: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「速率與排水時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Rate and drainage time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較剪切時間與排水尺度並監測孔壓，使用不同速度時保持相同飽和與邊界；試驗方案由專業人員選定，課程時間估算不能替代規範要求或直接成為設備速率設定。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：將未排水弱化歸因於表面磨耗會選錯殘餘參數，反之緩慢試驗的高阻力也不能代表快速卸荷；缺少孔壓資料時兩種機制很難分開。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare shearing duration with drainage scale while monitoring pressure, holding saturation and boundaries constant across rates; specialists select the test program, and this time estimate does not prescribe a machine rate or replace a standard. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Attributing undrained weakening to surface wear selects the wrong residual parameter, while slow-test resistance does not represent rapid unloading. Without pore-pressure records the mechanisms are difficult to distinguish. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄速率與排水時間的資料來源與適用條件。比較剪切時間與排水尺度並監測孔壓，使用不同速度時保持相同飽和與邊界；試驗方案由專業人員選定，課程時間估算不能替代規範要求或直接成為設備速率設定。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for rate and drainage time. Compare shearing duration with drainage scale while monitoring pressure, holding saturation and boundaries constant across rates; specialists select the test program, and this time estimate does not prescribe a machine rate or replace a standard.","failure":"注意干擾：將未排水弱化歸因於表面磨耗會選錯殘餘參數，反之緩慢試驗的高阻力也不能代表快速卸荷；缺少孔壓資料時兩種機制很難分開。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Attributing undrained weakening to surface wear selects the wrong residual parameter, while slow-test resistance does not represent rapid unloading. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較剪切時間與排水尺度並監測孔壓，使用不同速度時保持相同飽和與邊界；試驗方案由專業人員選定，課程時間估算不能替代規範要求或直接成為設備速率設定。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：將未排水弱化歸因於表面磨耗會選錯殘餘參數，反之緩慢試驗的高阻力也不能代表快速卸荷；缺少孔壓資料時兩種機制很難分開。","textEn":"Compare shearing duration with drainage scale while monitoring pressure, holding saturation and boundaries constant across rates; specialists select the test program, and this time estimate does not prescribe a machine rate or replace a standard. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Attributing undrained weakening to surface wear selects the wrong residual parameter, while slow-test resistance does not represent rapid unloading. Without pore-pressure records the mechanisms are difficult to distinguish.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄速率與排水時間的資料來源與適用條件。比較剪切時間與排水尺度並監測孔壓，使用不同速度時保持相同飽和與邊界；試驗方案由專業人員選定，課程時間估算不能替代規範要求或直接成為設備速率設定。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for rate and drainage time. Compare shearing duration with drainage scale while monitoring pressure, holding saturation and boundaries constant across rates; specialists select the test program, and this time estimate does not prescribe a machine rate or replace a standard.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「速率與排水時間」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Rate and drainage time\"?","options":["比較剪切時間與排水尺度並監測孔壓，使用不同速度時保持相同飽和與邊界；試驗方案由專業人員選定，課程時間估算不能替代規範要求或直接成為設備速率設定。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","只用單側位移計就能完全排除試件轉動造成的假剪脹。"],"optionsEn":["Compare shearing duration with drainage scale while monitoring pressure, holding saturation and boundaries constant across rates.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","One displacement gauge on one side completely excludes rocking-induced false dilation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"比較剪切時間與排水尺度並監測孔壓，使用不同速度時保持相同飽和與邊界；試驗方案由專業人員選定，課程時間估算不能替代規範要求或直接成為設備速率設定。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare shearing duration with drainage scale while monitoring pressure, holding saturation and boundaries constant across rates; specialists select the test program, and this time estimate does not prescribe a machine rate or replace a standard. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b131-v14-28","title":"速率與排水時間：失效診斷","titleEn":"Rate and drainage time: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「速率與排水時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Rate and drainage time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將未排水弱化歸因於表面磨耗會選錯殘餘參數，反之緩慢試驗的高阻力也不能代表快速卸荷；缺少孔壓資料時兩種機制很難分開。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Attributing undrained weakening to surface wear selects the wrong residual parameter, while slow-test resistance does not represent rapid unloading. Without pore-pressure records the mechanisms are difficult to distinguish. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：將未排水弱化歸因於表面磨耗會選錯殘餘參數，反之緩慢試驗的高阻力也不能代表快速卸荷；缺少孔壓資料時兩種機制很難分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Without pore-pressure records the mechanisms are difficult to distinguish.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要試驗速度很慢，就不必再檢查孔壓和排水。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A sufficiently slow test never needs pore-pressure or drainage checks.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將未排水弱化歸因於表面磨耗會選錯殘餘參數，反之緩慢試驗的高阻力也不能代表快速卸荷；缺少孔壓資料時兩種機制很難分開。","textEn":"Attributing undrained weakening to surface wear selects the wrong residual parameter, while slow-test resistance does not represent rapid unloading. Without pore-pressure records the mechanisms are difficult to distinguish.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「速率與排水時間」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Rate and drainage time\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","將未排水弱化歸因於表面磨耗會選錯殘餘參數，反之緩慢試驗的高阻力也不能代表快速卸荷；缺少孔壓資料時兩種機制很難分開。","一條高解析表面剖面足以代表所有方向和尺度的粗糙度。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Attributing undrained weakening to surface wear selects the wrong residual parameter, while slow-test resistance does not represent rapid unloading.","One high-resolution profile represents roughness in every direction and at every scale."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將未排水弱化歸因於表面磨耗會選錯殘餘參數，反之緩慢試驗的高阻力也不能代表快速卸荷；缺少孔壓資料時兩種機制很難分開。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Attributing undrained weakening to surface wear selects the wrong residual parameter, while slow-test resistance does not represent rapid unloading. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b131-v14-29","title":"粗糙度與尺度差：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Roughness and scale dependence: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「粗糙度與尺度差」如何影響岩體節理剪力試驗的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Roughness and scale dependence” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Rock-joint shear testing”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"小試件可被單一粗糙峰主導，大節理面則包含多種波長與接觸區。量測粗糙度要標明剖面方向和解析度，因為順層與橫層剪切可能呈現不同咬合，不能用一條剖面代表所有方向。 假設同高程差2 mm在10與100 mm基長上，平均坡度分別0.2與0.02；尺度改變使表觀坡度差10倍。 低解析掃描會抹去細峰，高解析噪訊又可能誇大粗糙度；若把不同濾波的指標混合比較，得到的強度差可能只是資料處理差異。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「粗糙度與尺度差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"One asperity may dominate a small specimen, while a large joint contains multiple wavelengths and contacts. Roughness profiles require direction and resolution because interlock differs by shearing direction; one trace cannot represent the entire surface. An assumed 2 mm height change over 10 and 100 mm baselines gives slopes 0.2 and 0.02, a tenfold apparent difference caused by scale. Coarse scanning removes fine asperities while high-resolution noise exaggerates roughness. Combining differently filtered indices can make a processing difference appear to be a genuine difference in shear resistance. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Roughness and scale dependence” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「一條高解析表面剖面足以代表所有方向和尺度的粗糙度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"One high-resolution profile represents roughness in every direction and at every scale.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「粗糙度與尺度差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Roughness and scale dependence”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-29-k1","title":"粗糙度與尺度差","titleEn":"Roughness and scale dependence","text":"小試件可被單一粗糙峰主導，大節理面則包含多種波長與接觸區。量測粗糙度要標明剖面方向和解析度，因為順層與橫層剪切可能呈現不同咬合，不能用一條剖面代表所有方向。","textEn":"One asperity may dominate a small specimen, while a large joint contains multiple wavelengths and contacts. Roughness profiles require direction and resolution because interlock differs by shearing direction; one trace cannot represent the entire surface.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：一條高解析表面剖面足以代表所有方向和尺度的粗糙度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: One high-resolution profile represents roughness in every direction and at every scale. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「粗糙度與尺度差」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Roughness and scale dependence\" is correct?","options":["一條高解析表面剖面足以代表所有方向和尺度的粗糙度。","力計精度就是整個節理抗剪應力試驗的不確定度。","小試件可被單一粗糙峰主導，大節理面則包含多種波長與接觸區。"],"optionsEn":["One high-resolution profile represents roughness in every direction and at every scale.","Load-cell accuracy equals the complete uncertainty of a joint shear-stress test.","One asperity may dominate a small specimen, while a large joint contains multiple wavelengths and contacts."],"answer":2,"explanation":"小試件可被單一粗糙峰主導，大節理面則包含多種波長與接觸區。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"One asperity may dominate a small specimen, while a large joint contains multiple wavelengths and contacts. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b131-v14-30","title":"粗糙度與尺度差：定量估算","titleEn":"Roughness and scale dependence: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「粗糙度與尺度差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Roughness and scale dependence” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設同高程差2 mm在10與100 mm基長上，平均坡度分別0.2與0.02；尺度改變使表觀坡度差10倍。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. An assumed 2 mm height change over 10 and 100 mm baselines gives slopes 0.2 and 0.02, a tenfold apparent difference caused by scale. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：沿預期剪切方向量測多條表面剖面，另以三維掃描查空間差異；報告點距、濾波與試件尺寸，使用經驗粗糙度模型時需明列其適用尺度和法向應力範圍。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure multiple profiles along expected shear direction and compare three-dimensional scans; report spacing, filtering and specimen size, explicitly bounding the scale and normal-stress range of any empirical roughness model.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設同高程差2 mm在10與100 mm基長上，平均坡度分別0.2與0.02；尺度改變使表觀坡度差10倍。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. An assumed 2 mm height change over 10 and 100 mm baselines gives slopes 0.2 and 0.02, a tenfold apparent difference caused by scale.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「粗糙度與尺度差」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Roughness and scale dependence\", which statement holds?","options":["以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","兩點擬合的線性摩擦包絡可以外推到任何法向應力。","定法向力與定法向剛度試驗必定得到同樣的曲線。"],"optionsEn":["The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","A linear friction envelope fitted to two points applies at any normal stress.","Constant-normal-load and constant-normal-stiffness tests necessarily produce the same curve."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b131-v14-31","title":"粗糙度與尺度差：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Roughness and scale dependence: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「粗糙度與尺度差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Roughness and scale dependence” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"沿預期剪切方向量測多條表面剖面，另以三維掃描查空間差異；報告點距、濾波與試件尺寸，使用經驗粗糙度模型時需明列其適用尺度和法向應力範圍。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：低解析掃描會抹去細峰，高解析噪訊又可能誇大粗糙度；若把不同濾波的指標混合比較，得到的強度差可能只是資料處理差異。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure multiple profiles along expected shear direction and compare three-dimensional scans; report spacing, filtering and specimen size, explicitly bounding the scale and normal-stress range of any empirical roughness model. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Coarse scanning removes fine asperities while high-resolution noise exaggerates roughness. Combining differently filtered indices can make a processing difference appear to be a genuine difference in shear resistance. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄粗糙度與尺度差的資料來源與適用條件。沿預期剪切方向量測多條表面剖面，另以三維掃描查空間差異；報告點距、濾波與試件尺寸，使用經驗粗糙度模型時需明列其適用尺度和法向應力範圍。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for roughness and scale dependence. Measure multiple profiles along expected shear direction and compare three-dimensional scans; report spacing, filtering and specimen size, explicitly bounding the scale and normal-stress range of any empirical roughness model.","failure":"注意干擾：低解析掃描會抹去細峰，高解析噪訊又可能誇大粗糙度；若把不同濾波的指標混合比較，得到的強度差可能只是資料處理差異。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Coarse scanning removes fine asperities while high-resolution noise exaggerates roughness. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"沿預期剪切方向量測多條表面剖面，另以三維掃描查空間差異；報告點距、濾波與試件尺寸，使用經驗粗糙度模型時需明列其適用尺度和法向應力範圍。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：低解析掃描會抹去細峰，高解析噪訊又可能誇大粗糙度；若把不同濾波的指標混合比較，得到的強度差可能只是資料處理差異。","textEn":"Measure multiple profiles along expected shear direction and compare three-dimensional scans; report spacing, filtering and specimen size, explicitly bounding the scale and normal-stress range of any empirical roughness model. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Coarse scanning removes fine asperities while high-resolution noise exaggerates roughness. Combining differently filtered indices can make a processing difference appear to be a genuine difference in shear resistance.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄粗糙度與尺度差的資料來源與適用條件。沿預期剪切方向量測多條表面剖面，另以三維掃描查空間差異；報告點距、濾波與試件尺寸，使用經驗粗糙度模型時需明列其適用尺度和法向應力範圍。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for roughness and scale dependence. Measure multiple profiles along expected shear direction and compare three-dimensional scans; report spacing, filtering and specimen size, explicitly bounding the scale and normal-stress range of any empirical roughness model.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「粗糙度與尺度差」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Roughness and scale dependence\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","沿預期剪切方向量測多條表面剖面，另以三維掃描查空間差異；報告點距、濾波與試件尺寸，使用經驗粗糙度模型時需明列其適用尺度和法向應力範圍。","試驗曲線的最後一點必定已代表真正殘餘強度。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Measure multiple profiles along expected shear direction and compare three-dimensional scans.","The final point of any test curve necessarily represents true residual strength."],"answer":1,"explanation":"沿預期剪切方向量測多條表面剖面，另以三維掃描查空間差異；報告點距、濾波與試件尺寸，使用經驗粗糙度模型時需明列其適用尺度和法向應力範圍。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure multiple profiles along expected shear direction and compare three-dimensional scans; report spacing, filtering and specimen size, explicitly bounding the scale and normal-stress range of any empirical roughness model. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b131-v14-32","title":"粗糙度與尺度差：失效診斷","titleEn":"Roughness and scale dependence: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「粗糙度與尺度差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Roughness and scale dependence” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"低解析掃描會抹去細峰，高解析噪訊又可能誇大粗糙度；若把不同濾波的指標混合比較，得到的強度差可能只是資料處理差異。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Coarse scanning removes fine asperities while high-resolution noise exaggerates roughness. Combining differently filtered indices can make a processing difference appear to be a genuine difference in shear resistance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：低解析掃描會抹去細峰，高解析噪訊又可能誇大粗糙度；若把不同濾波的指標混合比較，得到的強度差可能只是資料處理差異。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Combining differently filtered indices can make a processing difference appear to be a genuine difference in shear resistance.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「一條高解析表面剖面足以代表所有方向和尺度的粗糙度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"One high-resolution profile represents roughness in every direction and at every scale.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"低解析掃描會抹去細峰，高解析噪訊又可能誇大粗糙度；若把不同濾波的指標混合比較，得到的強度差可能只是資料處理差異。","textEn":"Coarse scanning removes fine asperities while high-resolution noise exaggerates roughness. Combining differently filtered indices can make a processing difference appear to be a genuine difference in shear resistance.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「粗糙度與尺度差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Roughness and scale dependence\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","力計精度就是整個節理抗剪應力試驗的不確定度。","低解析掃描會抹去細峰，高解析噪訊又可能誇大粗糙度；若把不同濾波的指標混合比較，得到的強度差可能只是資料處理差異。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Load-cell accuracy equals the complete uncertainty of a joint shear-stress test.","Coarse scanning removes fine asperities while high-resolution noise exaggerates roughness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"低解析掃描會抹去細峰，高解析噪訊又可能誇大粗糙度；若把不同濾波的指標混合比較，得到的強度差可能只是資料處理差異。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Coarse scanning removes fine asperities while high-resolution noise exaggerates roughness. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b131-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「量測誤差與強度」與「剪切功與試後證據」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Measurement error and strength\" and \"Shear work and post-test evidence\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b131-v14-33","title":"量測誤差與強度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Measurement error and strength: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「量測誤差與強度」如何影響岩體節理剪力試驗的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Measurement error and strength” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Rock-joint shear testing”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"力與面積的不確定性共同控制換算應力，摩擦角又透過非線性反正切求得。只報設備力計精度會漏掉天然表面尺寸、傾斜與法向控制誤差，須以完整誤差鏈說明結果。 假設力標準不確定2%、面積3%，獨立小誤差下應力相對不確定√(0.02²+0.03²)=3.61%。 只看小數位數會把統計不顯著差異解釋成地質分區，忽略相關誤差又使平方和估計過小；設計採值因此可能對不存在的差異過度反應。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「量測誤差與強度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Force and area uncertainty jointly control stress, while friction angle follows a nonlinear inverse tangent. Load-cell accuracy alone omits natural-surface dimensions, rocking and normal-control error, requiring the complete measurement chain. Assume independent small standard uncertainties of 2% in force and 3% in area; relative stress uncertainty is √(0.02²+0.03²)=3.61%. Decimal precision can make insignificant differences look like geological domains, while ignored correlation understates propagated uncertainty. Design may then respond strongly to distinctions unsupported by the measurements. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Measurement error and strength” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「力計精度就是整個節理抗剪應力試驗的不確定度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Load-cell accuracy equals the complete uncertainty of a joint shear-stress test.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「量測誤差與強度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Measurement error and strength”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-33-k1","title":"量測誤差與強度","titleEn":"Measurement error and strength","text":"力與面積的不確定性共同控制換算應力，摩擦角又透過非線性反正切求得。只報設備力計精度會漏掉天然表面尺寸、傾斜與法向控制誤差，須以完整誤差鏈說明結果。","textEn":"Force and area uncertainty jointly control stress, while friction angle follows a nonlinear inverse tangent. Load-cell accuracy alone omits natural-surface dimensions, rocking and normal-control error, requiring the complete measurement chain.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：力計精度就是整個節理抗剪應力試驗的不確定度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Load-cell accuracy equals the complete uncertainty of a joint shear-stress test. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「量測誤差與強度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Measurement error and strength\" is correct?","options":["力與面積的不確定性共同控制換算應力，摩擦角又透過非線性反正切求得。","力計精度就是整個節理抗剪應力試驗的不確定度。","剪切曲線下面積全部是目標節理轉成熱的摩擦能。"],"optionsEn":["Force and area uncertainty jointly control stress, while friction angle follows a nonlinear inverse tangent.","Load-cell accuracy equals the complete uncertainty of a joint shear-stress test.","All area under the shear curve is frictional heat generated at the intended joint."],"answer":0,"explanation":"力與面積的不確定性共同控制換算應力，摩擦角又透過非線性反正切求得。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Force and area uncertainty jointly control stress, while friction angle follows a nonlinear inverse tangent. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b131-v14-34","title":"量測誤差與強度：定量估算","titleEn":"Measurement error and strength: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「量測誤差與強度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Measurement error and strength” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設力標準不確定2%、面積3%，獨立小誤差下應力相對不確定√(0.02²+0.03²)=3.61%。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume independent small standard uncertainties of 2% in force and 3% in area; relative stress uncertainty is √(0.02²+0.03²)=3.61%. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用校準紀錄與重複尺寸量測估計不確定度，檢查面積和位移是否共享同一誤差來源；對關鍵強度參數做上下限分析，只有差異大於量測與試件散布時才主張材料確有變化。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Estimate uncertainty from calibration and repeated dimensions, checking shared error sources in area and displacement; bracket strength parameters and claim material differences only when they exceed measurement uncertainty and specimen variability.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設力標準不確定2%、面積3%，獨立小誤差下應力相對不確定√(0.02²+0.03²)=3.61%。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume independent small standard uncertainties of 2% in force and 3% in area; relative stress uncertainty is √(0.02²+0.03²)=3.61%.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「量測誤差與強度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Measurement error and strength\", which statement holds?","options":["外加法向荷重除面積就是含水節理的有效法向應力。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","只用單側位移計就能完全排除試件轉動造成的假剪脹。"],"optionsEn":["Applied normal load divided by area equals effective stress on a wet joint.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","One displacement gauge on one side completely excludes rocking-induced false dilation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b131-v14-35","title":"量測誤差與強度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Measurement error and strength: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「量測誤差與強度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Measurement error and strength” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用校準紀錄與重複尺寸量測估計不確定度，檢查面積和位移是否共享同一誤差來源；對關鍵強度參數做上下限分析，只有差異大於量測與試件散布時才主張材料確有變化。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：只看小數位數會把統計不顯著差異解釋成地質分區，忽略相關誤差又使平方和估計過小；設計採值因此可能對不存在的差異過度反應。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Estimate uncertainty from calibration and repeated dimensions, checking shared error sources in area and displacement; bracket strength parameters and claim material differences only when they exceed measurement uncertainty and specimen variability. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Decimal precision can make insignificant differences look like geological domains, while ignored correlation understates propagated uncertainty. Design may then respond strongly to distinctions unsupported by the measurements. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄量測誤差與強度的資料來源與適用條件。用校準紀錄與重複尺寸量測估計不確定度，檢查面積和位移是否共享同一誤差來源；對關鍵強度參數做上下限分析，只有差異大於量測與試件散布時才主張材料確有變化。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for measurement error and strength. Estimate uncertainty from calibration and repeated dimensions, checking shared error sources in area and displacement; bracket strength parameters and claim material differences only when they exceed measurement uncertainty and specimen variability.","failure":"注意干擾：只看小數位數會把統計不顯著差異解釋成地質分區，忽略相關誤差又使平方和估計過小；設計採值因此可能對不存在的差異過度反應。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Decimal precision can make insignificant differences look like geological domains, while ignored correlation understates propagated uncertainty. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用校準紀錄與重複尺寸量測估計不確定度，檢查面積和位移是否共享同一誤差來源；對關鍵強度參數做上下限分析，只有差異大於量測與試件散布時才主張材料確有變化。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：只看小數位數會把統計不顯著差異解釋成地質分區，忽略相關誤差又使平方和估計過小；設計採值因此可能對不存在的差異過度反應。","textEn":"Estimate uncertainty from calibration and repeated dimensions, checking shared error sources in area and displacement; bracket strength parameters and claim material differences only when they exceed measurement uncertainty and specimen variability. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Decimal precision can make insignificant differences look like geological domains, while ignored correlation understates propagated uncertainty. Design may then respond strongly to distinctions unsupported by the measurements.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄量測誤差與強度的資料來源與適用條件。用校準紀錄與重複尺寸量測估計不確定度，檢查面積和位移是否共享同一誤差來源；對關鍵強度參數做上下限分析，只有差異大於量測與試件散布時才主張材料確有變化。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for measurement error and strength. Estimate uncertainty from calibration and repeated dimensions, checking shared error sources in area and displacement; bracket strength parameters and claim material differences only when they exceed measurement uncertainty and specimen variability.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「量測誤差與強度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Measurement error and strength\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","剪切位移增加時，應力仍應永遠除以最初重疊面積。","用校準紀錄與重複尺寸量測估計不確定度，檢查面積和位移是否共享同一誤差來源；對關鍵強度參數做上下限分析，只有差異大於量測與試件散布時才主張材料確有變化。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Shear stress should always use initial overlap area as displacement increases.","Estimate uncertainty from calibration and repeated dimensions, checking shared error sources in area and displacement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用校準紀錄與重複尺寸量測估計不確定度，檢查面積和位移是否共享同一誤差來源；對關鍵強度參數做上下限分析，只有差異大於量測與試件散布時才主張材料確有變化。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Estimate uncertainty from calibration and repeated dimensions, checking shared error sources in area and displacement; bracket strength parameters and claim material differences only when they exceed measurement uncertainty and specimen variability. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b131-v14-36","title":"量測誤差與強度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Measurement error and strength: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「量測誤差與強度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Measurement error and strength” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只看小數位數會把統計不顯著差異解釋成地質分區，忽略相關誤差又使平方和估計過小；設計採值因此可能對不存在的差異過度反應。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Decimal precision can make insignificant differences look like geological domains, while ignored correlation understates propagated uncertainty. Design may then respond strongly to distinctions unsupported by the measurements. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只看小數位數會把統計不顯著差異解釋成地質分區，忽略相關誤差又使平方和估計過小；設計採值因此可能對不存在的差異過度反應。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Design may then respond strongly to distinctions unsupported by the measurements.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「力計精度就是整個節理抗剪應力試驗的不確定度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Load-cell accuracy equals the complete uncertainty of a joint shear-stress test.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只看小數位數會把統計不顯著差異解釋成地質分區，忽略相關誤差又使平方和估計過小；設計採值因此可能對不存在的差異過度反應。","textEn":"Decimal precision can make insignificant differences look like geological domains, while ignored correlation understates propagated uncertainty. Design may then respond strongly to distinctions unsupported by the measurements.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「量測誤差與強度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Measurement error and strength\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只看小數位數會把統計不顯著差異解釋成地質分區，忽略相關誤差又使平方和估計過小；設計採值因此可能對不存在的差異過度反應。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","剪切曲線下面積全部是目標節理轉成熱的摩擦能。"],"optionsEn":["Decimal precision can make insignificant differences look like geological domains, while ignored correlation understates propagated uncertainty.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","All area under the shear curve is frictional heat generated at the intended joint."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只看小數位數會把統計不顯著差異解釋成地質分區，忽略相關誤差又使平方和估計過小；設計採值因此可能對不存在的差異過度反應。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Decimal precision can make insignificant differences look like geological domains, while ignored correlation understates propagated uncertainty. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b131-v14-37","title":"剪切功與試後證據：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Shear work and post-test evidence: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「剪切功與試後證據」如何影響岩體節理剪力試驗的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Shear work and post-test evidence” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Rock-joint shear testing”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"剪切曲線下的面積表示單位面積做功，包含摩擦、粗糙峰破壞和設備儲能，並非全轉成可量測的熱。試後表面和碎屑讓能量解釋有物理依據，也揭露試體是否走錯破壞面。 假設平均剪應力0.6 MPa、滑移5 mm，W/A=τδ=3000 J/m²；未分離可回復儲能。 試件在膠結座或完整岩內破壞時，做功不能歸因於目標節理；若只留下最大剪力而丟失曲線與試後照片，後人無法辨認這種失真。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「剪切功與試後證據」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Area under the shear stress-displacement curve represents work per unit area, shared among friction, asperity damage and machine energy rather than entirely measured heat. Post-test surfaces and debris test that interpretation and identify unintended failure planes. With assumed mean shear stress 0.6 MPa and slip 5 mm, W/A=τδ=3000 J/m², without separating recoverable stored energy. Failure through the mounting material or intact rock invalidates attribution of work to the intended joint. Retaining only peak force and discarding curves and photographs prevents later detection of that error. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Shear work and post-test evidence” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「剪切曲線下面積全部是目標節理轉成熱的摩擦能。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"All area under the shear curve is frictional heat generated at the intended joint.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「剪切功與試後證據」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Shear work and post-test evidence”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-37-k1","title":"剪切功與試後證據","titleEn":"Shear work and post-test evidence","text":"剪切曲線下的面積表示單位面積做功，包含摩擦、粗糙峰破壞和設備儲能，並非全轉成可量測的熱。試後表面和碎屑讓能量解釋有物理依據，也揭露試體是否走錯破壞面。","textEn":"Area under the shear stress-displacement curve represents work per unit area, shared among friction, asperity damage and machine energy rather than entirely measured heat. Post-test surfaces and debris test that interpretation and identify unintended failure planes.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：剪切曲線下面積全部是目標節理轉成熱的摩擦能。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: All area under the shear curve is frictional heat generated at the intended joint. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「剪切功與試後證據」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Shear work and post-test evidence\" is correct?","options":["剪切曲線下面積全部是目標節理轉成熱的摩擦能。","剪切曲線下的面積表示單位面積做功，包含摩擦、粗糙峰破壞和設備儲能，並非全轉成可量測的熱。","兩點擬合的線性摩擦包絡可以外推到任何法向應力。"],"optionsEn":["All area under the shear curve is frictional heat generated at the intended joint.","Area under the shear stress-displacement curve represents work per unit area, shared among friction, asperity damage and machine energy rather than entirely measured heat.","A linear friction envelope fitted to two points applies at any normal stress."],"answer":1,"explanation":"剪切曲線下的面積表示單位面積做功，包含摩擦、粗糙峰破壞和設備儲能，並非全轉成可量測的熱。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Area under the shear stress-displacement curve represents work per unit area, shared among friction, asperity damage and machine energy rather than entirely measured heat. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b131-v14-38","title":"剪切功與試後證據：定量估算","titleEn":"Shear work and post-test evidence: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「剪切功與試後證據」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Shear work and post-test evidence” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設平均剪應力0.6 MPa、滑移5 mm，W/A=τδ=3000 J/m²；未分離可回復儲能。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. With assumed mean shear stress 0.6 MPa and slip 5 mm, W/A=τδ=3000 J/m², without separating recoverable stored energy. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：數值積分原始曲線並核對位移零點，試後拍攝上下表面與碎屑位置；交接時把能量、峰殘值和破壞路徑一起提供，由試驗及設計負責人確認是否代表目標節理。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Integrate the original curve with a checked displacement zero and photograph both surfaces and debris; hand over work, peak-residual values and failure path together for laboratory and design leads to judge representativeness.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設平均剪應力0.6 MPa、滑移5 mm，W/A=τδ=3000 J/m²；未分離可回復儲能。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. With assumed mean shear stress 0.6 MPa and slip 5 mm, W/A=τδ=3000 J/m², without separating recoverable stored energy.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「剪切功與試後證據」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Shear work and post-test evidence\", which statement holds?","options":["定法向力與定法向剛度試驗必定得到同樣的曲線。","試驗曲線的最後一點必定已代表真正殘餘強度。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["Constant-normal-load and constant-normal-stiffness tests necessarily produce the same curve.","The final point of any test curve necessarily represents true residual strength.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b131-v14-39","title":"剪切功與試後證據：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Shear work and post-test evidence: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「剪切功與試後證據」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Shear work and post-test evidence” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"數值積分原始曲線並核對位移零點，試後拍攝上下表面與碎屑位置；交接時把能量、峰殘值和破壞路徑一起提供，由試驗及設計負責人確認是否代表目標節理。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：試件在膠結座或完整岩內破壞時，做功不能歸因於目標節理；若只留下最大剪力而丟失曲線與試後照片，後人無法辨認這種失真。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Integrate the original curve with a checked displacement zero and photograph both surfaces and debris; hand over work, peak-residual values and failure path together for laboratory and design leads to judge representativeness. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Failure through the mounting material or intact rock invalidates attribution of work to the intended joint. Retaining only peak force and discarding curves and photographs prevents later detection of that error. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄剪切功與試後證據的資料來源與適用條件。數值積分原始曲線並核對位移零點，試後拍攝上下表面與碎屑位置；交接時把能量、峰殘值和破壞路徑一起提供，由試驗及設計負責人確認是否代表目標節理。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for shear work and post-test evidence. Integrate the original curve with a checked displacement zero and photograph both surfaces and debris; hand over work, peak-residual values and failure path together for laboratory and design leads to judge representativeness.","failure":"注意干擾：試件在膠結座或完整岩內破壞時，做功不能歸因於目標節理；若只留下最大剪力而丟失曲線與試後照片，後人無法辨認這種失真。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Failure through the mounting material or intact rock invalidates attribution of work to the intended joint. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"數值積分原始曲線並核對位移零點，試後拍攝上下表面與碎屑位置；交接時把能量、峰殘值和破壞路徑一起提供，由試驗及設計負責人確認是否代表目標節理。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：試件在膠結座或完整岩內破壞時，做功不能歸因於目標節理；若只留下最大剪力而丟失曲線與試後照片，後人無法辨認這種失真。","textEn":"Integrate the original curve with a checked displacement zero and photograph both surfaces and debris; hand over work, peak-residual values and failure path together for laboratory and design leads to judge representativeness. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Failure through the mounting material or intact rock invalidates attribution of work to the intended joint. Retaining only peak force and discarding curves and photographs prevents later detection of that error.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄剪切功與試後證據的資料來源與適用條件。數值積分原始曲線並核對位移零點，試後拍攝上下表面與碎屑位置；交接時把能量、峰殘值和破壞路徑一起提供，由試驗及設計負責人確認是否代表目標節理。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for shear work and post-test evidence. Integrate the original curve with a checked displacement zero and photograph both surfaces and debris; hand over work, peak-residual values and failure path together for laboratory and design leads to judge representativeness.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「剪切功與試後證據」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Shear work and post-test evidence\"?","options":["數值積分原始曲線並核對位移零點，試後拍攝上下表面與碎屑位置；交接時把能量、峰殘值和破壞路徑一起提供，由試驗及設計負責人確認是否代表目標節理。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","只要試驗速度很慢，就不必再檢查孔壓和排水。"],"optionsEn":["Integrate the original curve with a checked displacement zero and photograph both surfaces and debris.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A sufficiently slow test never needs pore-pressure or drainage checks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"數值積分原始曲線並核對位移零點，試後拍攝上下表面與碎屑位置；交接時把能量、峰殘值和破壞路徑一起提供，由試驗及設計負責人確認是否代表目標節理。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Integrate the original curve with a checked displacement zero and photograph both surfaces and debris; hand over work, peak-residual values and failure path together for laboratory and design leads to judge representativeness. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b131-v14-40","title":"剪切功與試後證據：失效診斷","titleEn":"Shear work and post-test evidence: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b131-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「剪切功與試後證據」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Shear work and post-test evidence” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"試件在膠結座或完整岩內破壞時，做功不能歸因於目標節理；若只留下最大剪力而丟失曲線與試後照片，後人無法辨認這種失真。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Failure through the mounting material or intact rock invalidates attribution of work to the intended joint. Retaining only peak force and discarding curves and photographs prevents later detection of that error. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：試件在膠結座或完整岩內破壞時，做功不能歸因於目標節理；若只留下最大剪力而丟失曲線與試後照片，後人無法辨認這種失真。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Retaining only peak force and discarding curves and photographs prevents later detection of that error.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「剪切曲線下面積全部是目標節理轉成熱的摩擦能。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"All area under the shear curve is frictional heat generated at the intended joint.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b131-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"試件在膠結座或完整岩內破壞時，做功不能歸因於目標節理；若只留下最大剪力而丟失曲線與試後照片，後人無法辨認這種失真。","textEn":"Failure through the mounting material or intact rock invalidates attribution of work to the intended joint. Retaining only peak force and discarding curves and photographs prevents later detection of that error.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b131-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「剪切功與試後證據」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Shear work and post-test evidence\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","試件在膠結座或完整岩內破壞時，做功不能歸因於目標節理；若只留下最大剪力而丟失曲線與試後照片，後人無法辨認這種失真。","兩點擬合的線性摩擦包絡可以外推到任何法向應力。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Failure through the mounting material or intact rock invalidates attribution of work to the intended joint.","A linear friction envelope fitted to two points applies at any normal stress."],"answer":1,"explanation":"試件在膠結座或完整岩內破壞時，做功不能歸因於目標節理；若只留下最大剪力而丟失曲線與試後照片，後人無法辨認這種失真。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Failure through the mounting material or intact rock invalidates attribution of work to the intended joint. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v14s-isrm-methods","v14s-geo3","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"curriculumVersion":14,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
